rar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos al límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede ser una decisión basada en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen uniformemente en el tiempo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 101 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 7.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 14.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 9.5 to 21.1. December accounts for 5% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 8. Contract [1], for 14,999 euros, was awarded in December 2024.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts [1] and [2] to see if they align with the December trend. Review awardee A's contracts to determine if multiple contracts serve the same need. Look for repeated orders to assess if the same supplier was repeatedly chosen for similar services.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["%2FHLsaYOlnrlWhbmkna2nXQ%3D%3D","K8yNLhioCoWFlFRHfEzEaw%3D%3D","StR8dOp4NIvXOjazN1Dw9Q%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}